<title>USA: Shell says fire extinguished at Illinois refinery.</title>
<headline>Shell says fire extinguished at Illinois refinery.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Shell Oil Co refinery spokesman said a fire has been extinguished at a gasoline processing unit at its 268,000 barrel per day Wood River, Ill., refinery.</p>
<p>The fire broke out Tuesday in a &quot;gas plant&quot; at the refinery, he said, but additional information on the blaze and its impact on production was not immediately available. There were no injuries, the spokesman said.</p>
</text>
